  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), HFR's answer to a private message link that names a message: `forum2.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=prive&post=<N>&page=1&numreponse=<M>` (logged in, participant).\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: the answer (status, `Location`, final page) to the R25 shape on a private conversation, for a message on page 1 and for one on a later page.\n\nWhy: R25 shows a public topic answering `page=1&numreponse=M` with a 301 to its canonical path; private conversations have no known canonical path, and the corpus has no `cat=prive` link with a non-zero `numreponse` (MP list rows carry `numreponse=0`). LOT-137 follows LOT-095's router rule (no page, R25-shaped request) for such a link posted in a message; whether HFR redirects, serves page 1, or refuses is not known.\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); one PR per batch of captures.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-137 (#227), LOT-095 (#187)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n",
